<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17421" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλ-ητικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for the flute,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ap.</u>
				27b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάκτυλοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.Com.
					211
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλαμος</span>”
				<i>used for making flutes,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>HP</u>
					4.10.1
				</span></i>
			, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				221ix12
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plot.
					1.4.15
				</span></i>
			:<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>), ἡ,
				<i>flute-playing,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				501e
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1447a15
			</span></i>. Adv.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς, δεῖ καρκινοῦν τοὺς δακτύλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antiph.
					55.15
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.404f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fitted for flute playing,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Hp.Mi.</u>
					375b
				</span></i>
			 (
				Comp.
			).</div>
